  "notes": "The README says Defaults populate missing optional attributes with their default values, so the objects with c = 1, 2 and 3 should all get b = true. hashicorp/hcl's Defaults.apply (ext/typeexpr/defaults.go) unifies the elements of each list value after applying defaults (unifyAsSlice) and keeps them as a tuple when that fails. The objects get b while the null elements don't, so the list holding c = 1 and null becomes a tuple, and so do the second and third elements of v: a tuple holding that tuple and a list, and a tuple holding two lists whose object types differ. The elements of v, a null list and these two tuples, then unify through go-cty's UnifyUnsafe (unifyTuplesAsList in cty/convert/unify.go) to a list of lists of object({c = number}), the one candidate that every element converts to, unsafely, by dropping b. Both tuples convert to it, and the final conversion gives b back as null.",
